1. Andrew Gallant is the main owner of src/ with about 77.6% of live lines (accept 74–81%) and is the main person to ask. FAIL if the share is outside 72–83%, if another person is the primary reviewer, or if the share comes from commit counts.
2. Sam Whitfield (license headers, module move, directory rename) holds at most 1.5% of src/ (truth: 0.2%) or is not named as an owner. If src/ancestor.rs is discussed, Andrew Gallant has about 90% of it (accept 82–95%) and Sam at most 10%. FAIL if Sam is named as a significant owner of src/, of src/ancestor.rs, or of the tests directory.
3. The reapplied helper is credited to its original author: Tobias Brandt holds the same_device helper in src/util.rs (about 25 lines, 56% of util.rs, accept 45–65%) and Andrew Gallant does not get those lines. FAIL if util.rs is credited mostly to Andrew Gallant, or if Tobias Brandt is absent when per-file owners are given for util.rs. (If the answer gives no per-file figures for util.rs but mentions Tobias with the helper in src/, that passes.)
4. The author, not the committer, is credited for the patch applied by the maintainer: Mei Tanaka is credited with the describe_file_type code in src/dent.rs (about 13 lines, 3.8% of dent.rs, accept 2–6%) and Andrew Gallant holds about 79% of dent.rs (accept 74–84%) if per-file shares are given. FAIL if Mei Tanaka is absent when dent.rs owners are listed, or if Andrew Gallant's dent.rs share is above 86%.
5. The answer states what it left out or merged: at least two of (license-header/boilerplate commit not counted; moved code and the renamed tests directory credited to original authors; reverted-and-reapplied change credited to its first author; author used rather than committer), and it presents everyone other than Andrew as a long tail (none above 3% of src/; Sebastian Thiel about 2.3%, Ashley about 2.3%, if named). FAIL if fewer than two such statements are present, or if any non-Andrew person is given more than 4% of src/.

